    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ce287dd_3f469bc7",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/pwm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-28T05:22:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using DCR \u003e CTR to disable the PWM is stated in our datasheet. And I have discussed this with my Israeli colleagues. They also confirmed it.\n\nYou\u0027re right. We should remove the dependence between pwm_enable()/pwm_get_enabled() and pwm_set_raw_duty()/pwm_get_raw_duty().",
      "parentUuid": "5f15122e_baaa251d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "6588ca874cb65b6fe242d0c83910715ddbdcbf1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "265faac2_440ffe15",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/pwm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-28T16:59:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then, can you fix pwm_get_enabled and pwm_enable? The definition of \u0027enable\u0027 is currently blurry.",
      "parentUuid": "6ce287dd_3f469bc7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "6588ca874cb65b6fe242d0c83910715ddbdcbf1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82d15a10_f4af1efc",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/pwm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T00:57:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I don\u0027t get your point. Setting bit 7 in PWMCTL is necessary. Or its input clock will be disabled. Could you give me more detail about this? Thanks.",
      "parentUuid": "265faac2_440ffe15",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "6588ca874cb65b6fe242d0c83910715ddbdcbf1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b598eda1_cbb1cb10",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/pwm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T01:23:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For example, should pwm_get_enabled return false if NPCX_DCR(mdl) \u003e NPCX_CTR(mdl)?\n\nShould pwm_enable(x, 0) set NPCX_DCR(mdl) \u003d NPCX_CTR(mdl) + 1?\n\nWhat should \u0027enable\u0027 mean now? Is it just NPCX_PWMCTL(mdl) \u0026 NPCX_PWMCTL_PWR or NPCX_DCR(mdl) \u003e NPCX_CTR(mdl) or both?",
      "parentUuid": "82d15a10_f4af1efc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "6588ca874cb65b6fe242d0c83910715ddbdcbf1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c98c1724_79029a41",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/pwm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T02:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please refer Figure. 24 in npcx5\u0027s datasheet. Setting DCR \u003e CTR means that the result of 16-bits comparator is always false. It equals the duty cycle is zero. And setting bit 7 in PWMCTL means turn off all input clock sources of PWM module. Its output only relies on INVP bit.\n\nI think the explanation in commit message is not good enough. I\u0027ll update it later.",
      "parentUuid": "b598eda1_cbb1cb10",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "6588ca874cb65b6fe242d0c83910715ddbdcbf1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd538201_8f385ab5",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/pwm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T17:09:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, what\u0027s the answer to the first case? Should pwm_get_enabled return false if DCR \u003e CTR?",
      "parentUuid": "c98c1724_79029a41",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "6588ca874cb65b6fe242d0c83910715ddbdcbf1f",
